{{also|Erwürgen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|erwürgen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|irwurgen}}. Equivalent to {{prefix|de|er|würgen|t2=to choke}}. The main sense has always been “strangle”. In Early Modern German it was generalised to “kill, murder”, but this use was shortlived.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ɛʁˈvʏʁɡən/|[ʔɛɐ̯ˈvʏɐ̯.ɡŋ̍]}}
* {{audio|de|De-erwürgen.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[strangle]] {{gloss|choke someone to death}}
#: {{syn|de|erdrosseln}}
# {{lb|de|obsolete}} to [[kill]] violently, to [[slay]], [[murder]] {{defdate|chiefly 16th c.}}

